.TH MAKE 1
.SH NAME
make \- remake files from the rules of a makefile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B make
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-nksBir ]
.RB [ \-j1 ]
.RI [ var = value ...]
.RI [ target ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B make
is POSIX make with GNU make's common additions, with
.BR cc (1)
as its compiler. The makefile
.RB ( \-f 's,
else
.BR makefile ,
else
.BR Makefile )
is read whole: variables, explicit, pattern and suffix rules, includes.
Each goal (the command line's, else
.BR .DEFAULT_GOAL ,
else the first target that does not start with
.BR . )
is made depth first: its prerequisites, then its recipe if it is
missing, older than one of them, a prerequisite was remade, it is phony,
or
.BR \-B .
.PP
Each recipe line runs alone as
.BI "sh \-c " line
in make's folder, after it is shown (unless
.BR @ ,
.B \-s
or
.BR .SILENT ).
A status other than 0 stops make with
.B make: *** [target] Error N
and status 2.
.PP
Built in:
.BR "CC = cc" ,
the rules
.BR "%.o: %.c" ,
.BR "%.o: %.S" ,
.BR "%.o: %.s" ,
.BR "%: %.c" ,
.BR "%: %.o" .
Functions:
.BR subst ,
.BR patsubst ,
.BR strip ,
.BR findstring ,
.BR filter ,
.BR filter-out ,
.BR sort ,
.BR word ,
.BR words ,
.BR firstword ,
.BR lastword ,
.BR dir ,
.BR notdir ,
.BR suffix ,
.BR basename ,
.BR addsuffix ,
.BR addprefix ,
.BR wildcard ,
.BR foreach ,
.BR if ,
.BR call ,
.BR info ,
.BR warning ,
.BR error .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read this makefile (several may be given).
.TP
.BI \-C " dir"
Go to
.I dir
first.
.TP
.B \-n
Show the recipes, run none (lines with
.B $(MAKE)
still run).
.TP
.B \-k
Keep going: make the targets that do not depend on a failed one.
.TP
.B \-s
Silent: do not show the recipes.
.TP
.B \-B
Remake everything.
.TP
.B \-i
Ignore errors.
.TP
.B \-r
No built-in rules.
.TP
.BI \-j n
Accepted; one job runs at a time.
.TP
.IB var = value
Wins over the makefile's assignment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every goal was made; 2 on an error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /src/hello-make
a small project to try;
.B /src/sieos
SIEOS's own hello, sh and make, which build on SIEOS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
No conditionals
.RB ( ifeq ,
.BR ifdef ),
.BR define ,
.BR override ,
.BR vpath ,
target-specific variables,
.B $(shell)
or
.BR != ;
no
.BR \-q ,
.B \-t
or long options. A recipe line is one shell command: the shell has no
.BR ; ,
.BR && ,
.B |
or lasting
.BR cd .
